    "body": "partial fix on issue/31-wasm-ui-shell · draft PR #841 (`Refs #31`, does not close) · pinned by `file_dialog::tests::file_dialog_builder_keeps_every_setting`, `clock::tests::clock_seam_is_monotonic_and_does_duration_math` (plus the moved `shell_window::redraw_tests`) · merges at the next cut (feat).\n\nRung 2 is done: **camcraft-ui.wasm now builds and links for wasm32-unknown-unknown** (`web/build-app-wasm.sh` links it after rung 1's camcraft-cli.wasm). Three seams made that possible:\n- `egui_app/shell.rs` is split. The native winit loop, window and GPU bring-up are now `shell_window.rs` + `shell_window/frame.rs`, cfg'd off wasm32. `shell.rs` keeps the shared frame (`shell_layout`, dock tabs, viewport panel).\n- `crate::file_dialog` replaces the 13 `rfd::FileDialog` sites. On wasm32 it answers None (cancelled) with a diagnostic.\n- `camcraft_app::clock::Instant` uses web_time's Instant on wasm32. web-time was already in the lock.\n\nNative gate green: quick fell back to batch, 9/9 steps, clippy clean. The in-browser run was **not** exercised: there is no browser runner yet, and on wasm32 the entry refuses the windowed path by name.\n\nStill owed for \"UI runs in a browser\":\n1. A browser runner (eframe web runner or egui web glue) that calls `shell::shell_layout`.\n2. Async GPU bring-up for the `pollster::block_on` sites (gpu.rs, trace.rs, trace/composite.rs, headless_gpu.rs).\n3. An async file picker behind `file_dialog`.\n4. Run-inline fallbacks for the `std::thread::spawn` sites.\n5. The JS shim for the nine wasi imports, wasm-bindgen CLI 0.2.129, the page, and the in-browser CI job.\n6. Splitting the viewport panel out of `shell.rs`, which is still 923 lines.\n\nDetails are in docs/decisions/31-wasm-ui-shell.md.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
