    "body": "partial fix on issue/31-wasm-web-runner · draft PR #847 (`Refs #31`, does not close; stacked on #841) · pinned by `view_pass::tests::target_extent_is_never_zero_and_scales_with_the_pixel_ratio`, `view_pass::tests::a_browser_frame_with_no_egui_timer_still_follows_the_document` · merges at the next cut (feat), after #841.\n\nRung 3 is done: **the shell runs in a browser.**\n- `egui_app/shell_web.rs` is the browser shell: eframe's web runner over a canvas, drawing the same `shell_layout` frame and the same 3D pass as the native window (now shared in `egui_app/view_pass.rs`).\n- The blocking GPU waits have awaited twins (`TracePass`, `Composite`, `StockEye`, `headless_gpu`); the blocking forms and `pollster` are native-only.\n- `web/build-app-wasm.sh` now also runs wasm-bindgen and lays out `target/web/` with `web/index.html` and `web/wasi_shim.js` (the nine WASI imports).\n\nWhat ran: headless Chrome (WebGL2 through SwiftShader) loaded the page from a loopback server. The module instantiated, flecs built the world, the first frame drew (ribbon, browser tree, viewport with axes and view cube, properties, status line), and a click on the ribbon's Stock door opened the Stock page.\n\nNative gate green: quick fell back to batch, 9/9 steps, 35.3 min, clippy clean.\n\nNot exercised: WebGPU (Chrome offered no adapter here, so the awaited stock eye was refused by name before its await); anything past the first frame and one click; a release build; the `wasm` CI job.\n\nStill owed for \"Done means\":\n1. An async file picker behind `file_dialog` (nothing can be opened or saved in the browser yet).\n2. An inline playback path where the worker cannot spawn (it refuses by name today), and a browser check of import and generate.\n3. The in-browser CI job (manual trigger) and the Pages deployment (#688).\n4. A WebGPU run.\n5. Gating the 17 native-only helpers so `lib.rs` can drop its wasm32 `allow(dead_code)`.\n6. Splitting the viewport panel out of `shell.rs` (still 923 lines).\n\nDetails are in docs/decisions/31-wasm-web-runner.md.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
