    "body": "review fixes on issue/31-wasm-web-runner · PR #847 (draft, base `main` now; was stacked on #841) · head `b6483d66` · pinned by `diag::tests::shared_ui_code_prints_only_through_the_diag_seam` and the extended `view_pass::tests::target_extent_is_never_zero_and_scales_with_the_pixel_ratio` · merges at the next cut (feat).\n\nFixed from the review of `1f903bd4`:\n1. Diagnostics reach the browser console. `crates/ui/src/diag.rs` is the UI crate's one seam (`diag_warn!` / `diag_info!`): stderr / stdout natively, `console.warn` / `console.log` on wasm32. The stock eye's fall-back, the file dialog's \"cancelled\" note and the other direct prints in browser-compiled UI code go through it (35 sites, 12 files); a law test fails on a new direct print.\n2. `poll_oneoff` in `web/wasi_shim.js` now succeeds at once, reports clock subscriptions as elapsed and writes the skipped wait to the console. It used to answer ENOSYS under a comment that said otherwise.\n3. `web/build-app-wasm.sh`: the missing-imports message prints under pipefail.\n4. The wasm-bindgen install is announced before it runs, and `CAMCRAFT_WASM_NO_INSTALL=1` refuses it with instructions.\n5. The shim answers exactly the nine imports; unknown clocks and closed descriptors answer a named errno with one console warning each.\n6. The first browser target uses the same pixel-ratio clamp as every later frame (now inside `view_pass::target_extent`).\n\nGate green on `b6483d66` (quick fell back to batch, 9/9 steps, 55.3 min, clippy clean). `web/build-app-wasm.sh` exited 0, and headless Chrome drew the first frame again with the stock-eye refusal as a console warning.\n\nNot shown in the browser: the exact `eye.rs` \"CPU march stands in\" line. On WebGL2 the composite refuses first, so that line is never reached; it uses the same macro as the line that did appear. `poll_oneoff` was not called at start-up; the shim was checked in Node against a fake memory. The `CAMCRAFT_WASM_NO_INSTALL=1` refusal was not run.\n\nNew owed item: camcraft-app's own diagnostics (its `tracing` events and direct prints) are still dropped in a browser and need a console writer installed by the browser shell.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
